# Copy to gate-patterns.local and fill in with YOUR machine's identifiers.
# gate-patterns.local is git-ignored and must never be shipped: a scanner that
# embeds the strings it hunts for is itself the leak. Found exactly that way,
# 2026-09-07, when the gate refused a source tarball because it contained the gate.
#
# STRICT <regex>  — never legitimate in any file
# BINARY <regex>  — enforced only on binaries we build (legitimate in docs)
STRICT <your-username>
STRICT <your-lan-ip>
STRICT <your-server-ip>
STRICT <any-test-password>
BINARY /home/[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+/
